Description: In a 3D project a 2D element is in both eyes, and the monitors work at full eye resolution
 "Faked 3D becomes stereo by doubling": in a 3D project (its packing from its
 clips, one of them 3D) a 2D clip, title, still or colour is the same picture in
 both eyes, at the screen plane, through MLT's stereo3d_unpack packing=mono as
 the first filter of its timeline producer; colours, stills and titles get
 timeline producers of their own there, and every clip's timeline instances
 follow when the project becomes 3D or stops being, and once more when it has
 finished opening. Both monitors work on the project's frame of two eyes, each
 a whole picture of the project's resolution (the monitors' profile twice as
 wide, of twice the display aspect; "full is the layout, not a size"); the clip
 monitor makes it from the clip's own picture, so its 3D, left-eye and off
 views are of that frame. The render keeps adding the filter to a 2D producer
 that lacks it.
